\par }{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2688915 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2688915 The latest in the series of battlefield visits led by Colonel Oliver Warman
 (Balliol; late Welsh Guards) will take us to the northern Ardennes, and to the site of the allied crossing of the Rhine at Remagen Bridge. Oliver gives us as the theme of this visit \'ab\~The Beginning of the End\~\'bb
.  Interestingly, for those fascinated by the Appeasement movement, Oliver also plans to take us also to Bad Godesburg in the footsteps of Neville Chamberlain, a site symbolic of a period which might be tagged the Beginning of the Beginning. 
\par 
\par Our visit will take place on Friday 16}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033\insrsid2688915 th}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2688915 -Sunday 18}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033\insrsid2688915 th}{
\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2688915  October.   The party will leave the Gare du Nord at 8.25 a.m. on the Friday, arriving at K\'f6
ln at 12.15 p.m.  The party will be met by a private transfer bus to our hotel in the centre of the Old Town, the Maritim Hotel. At 2 p.m. our Coach leaves the hotel for
 the first part of the tour, returning that evening.  Then the Saturday part of the tour will be an all-day affair, finishing with a Rhine Steamer cruise in the late afternoon, hopefully before  G\'f6tterd\'e4mmerung sets in.
\par 
\par The party return to Paris by the 3.44 p.m. train on Sunday 18}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033\insrsid2688915 th}{\fs24\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033\insrsid2688915  October, arriving at the Gare du Nord at 7.35 p.m.
\par 
